Subject: [PATCH] layout: synchronize group members after exchanging spaces

ITarget::swap exchanges the group targets' spaces directly, without using
CWindowGroupTarget::assignToSpace. The original onUpdateSpace forwards the
update to member targets that still have their old ghost spaces, moving the
windows back to the old workspace while the group's layout stays on the new
one. Destroying that now-empty workspace leaves the group's space with an
expired parent; floating-to-tiled then dereferences it in dwindle addTarget.

Synchronize mismatched member spaces using the normal group workspace update
before forwarding onUpdateSpace. Leave already-synchronized groups alone and
preserve the original member updates.

Related: https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/issues/10342
AI-assisted: authored and tested with gpt-6.1-sol via Hermes Agent.
Remove when the packaged Hyprland release includes equivalent synchronization.

--- a/src/layout/target/WindowGroupTarget.cpp
+++ b/src/layout/target/WindowGroupTarget.cpp
@@ -81,4 +81,19 @@
 void CWindowGroupTarget::onUpdateSpace() {
+    const auto SPACE     = space();
+    const auto WORKSPACE = SPACE ? SPACE->workspace() : nullptr;
+
+    // Swaps exchange group spaces without going through assignToSpace. Bring
+    // members' ghost spaces along before their updates consult the old space.
+    if (WORKSPACE) {
+        for (const auto& w : m_group->windows()) {
+            if (w->m_target->space() == SPACE)
+                continue;
+
+            m_group->updateWorkspace(WORKSPACE);
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+
     for (const auto& w : m_group->windows()) {
         w->m_target->onUpdateSpace();
     }
